      "description": "Kirti Mandir is a birthplace of Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi and a small museum in the city of Porbandar, Gujarat, India. The museum displays some old photographs and books library. In this library of books written by Gandhi or relating to his philosophies.\nThe Mahatma Gandhi was born on 2 October 1869 in the ancestral house of the Gandhi family.\nThe Kirti Mandir is the main tourist attraction of the town. Many tourists comes to visit Kirti Mandir. \n\nThere are life-size oil paintings of Mahatma Gandhi and his wife Kasturba Gandhi side by side in the centre of Kirti Mandir. The place where Mahatma Gandhi was born is marked with a swastika for identification.",
